export const html = "<h1 id=\"chapter-2--content-lifecycle\">Chapter 2 · Content Lifecycle</h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How a fact gets into Overhype.me in the first place — the two ways a fact\nis submitted (a signed-in user writes one, or an admin/external system\nimports a batch) and the one funnel both feed into. What happens once a\nfact is in the queue is\n<a href=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\"><code>3-moderation.md</code></a>'s chapter, not this one.</p>\n<p>Deep spec: <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/moderation-workflow.md#the-ingestion-funnel--one-entrance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>moderation-workflow.md</code></a>.\nRationale history: <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/decisions.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>decisions.md</code></a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"what-it-does\">What it does</h2>\n<p>A fact is submitted exactly two ways — a signed-in user submits one, or an\nadmin (or an external system, via API key) imports a batch — and both land in\nthe same place: a <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#pending-review\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">pending review</a>, not the live catalogue. There is no third\nsource and no shortcut in the product itself: nothing in the running\napplication can create a fact directly outside this funnel. (Offline dev/ops\ntooling — a database seed script, a reseed utility — can insert facts\ndirectly; that's maintenance tooling, not a product ingestion path, and this\nchapter doesn't cover it.) That single funnel is what lets\n<a href=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\"><code>3-moderation.md</code></a> describe one review process and mean it for\nevery fact, regardless of how it arrived.</p>\n<p>This chapter covers the two entrances themselves — what a <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#submitter\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">submitter</a> sees, what\nan importer sends — and the cheap, pre-review checks each route runs before a fact ever reaches a human.\nWhat happens after that hand-off (<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#triage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">triage</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#enrichment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">enrichment</a>, the <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#visual-concept\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">Visual Concept</a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#test-renders\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">Test Renders</a> gates, publication) belongs to <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#moderation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">moderation</a> and taxonomy, and\nthis chapter links out rather than repeating it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2>\n<h3 id=\"for-the-submitter-writing-a-fact\">For the submitter (writing a fact)</h3>\n<p>Submitting is a two-step form: <strong>write</strong>, then <strong><a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#preview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">preview</a></strong>. While the\nsubmitter is writing, a <strong><a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#duplicate-detection\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">duplicate check</a></strong> runs automatically in the\nbackground — no button needed — comparing the draft against existing facts\nand, when the AI judges it the same fact or joke as one already there,\nshowing that match so the submitter can decide for themselves whether to\ncontinue. It's advisory only: nothing stops a submission that's flagged. The\nwarning is only a preview, tied to the exact text on screen — editing the\ntext, or the template on Preview, drops it and checks again. What the\nmoderator sees doesn't depend on it: after the submission is saved, the\nserver checks the saved wording itself and stores the verdict on the review.</p>\n<p>Moving from Write to Preview is a different kind of step — a <strong>required,\nblocking</strong> one. Clicking Preview sends the draft through a <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#grammar-pass\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">grammar pass</a> that\nresolves the fact's <code>{NAME}</code> and pronoun <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#personalization-tokens\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">placeholders</a> into a preview across\nexample names and <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#pronoun-set\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">pronoun sets</a>, so the submitter can catch an awkward\nconjugation before sending it in. A failed pass leaves the submitter on\nWrite with an error rather than letting them continue; only a successful one\nreaches Preview.</p>\n<p>That normal path to Preview also fetches AI-suggested <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#hashtags\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">hashtags</a> to pre-fill\nthe (editable) hashtags field — a non-blocking suggestion the submitter can\nkeep, edit, or clear. (A submitter picking up an <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#autosaved-draft\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">autosaved draft</a> skips\nstraight to Preview with their saved template and doesn't trigger a fresh\nsuggestion fetch.)</p>\n<p>Submitting requires being signed in with an account that has verified its\nemail and completed <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#onboarding\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">onboarding</a> — the one-time screen every account\nfinishes before it can act at all (see\n<a href=\"/admin/help/9-accounts-and-auth#verify-then-onboard-then-act\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/9-accounts-and-auth#verify-then-onboard-then-act\">chapter 9</a>). Onboarding\nincludes a Turnstile challenge, so an onboarded account is not challenged\nagain when it submits. On submit, the server\nre-normalizes the fact's grammar independently of what the client already\nchecked — a submission that reached the server without going through the\nWrite-to-Preview grammar pass (an API client, a stale front-end) still gets\nthe same cleanup applied, so every fact that reaches the <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#review-queue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">review queue</a> has\nbeen through the same grammar pass regardless of how it arrived. (One\nsubmitter's own pending facts are also protected from flooding the queue —\nsee <em>Boundaries &#x26; known limitations</em> below.)</p>\n<p>Successful submission notifies admins and logs an <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#activity-feed\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">activity-feed</a> entry for\nthe submitter, who is later notified again when their fact clears or is\nrejected.</p>\n<h3 id=\"for-the-admin-bulk-import\">For the admin (bulk import)</h3>\n<p>Bulk import exists in two forms that both do the same thing — turn a batch\nof fact texts into pending reviews — with different callers in mind:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>From the <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#admin-console\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">admin console</a></strong>, an admin pastes facts as JSON, CSV, or one\nfact per line and imports them in one action.</li>\n<li><strong>Via API key</strong>, an external system posts the same kind of batch\nprogrammatically, with an optional dry-run mode that validates without\nwriting anything.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Both paths run every text through the same grammar normalizer a user\nsubmission uses, so an imported fact's stored text is cleaned up identically\nto a hand-submitted one — though the rows aren't otherwise identical: an\nadmin-console import attributes the acting admin as submitter and always\nqueues an empty hashtag list; an API-key import has no submitter at all but\ncan carry caller-chosen hashtags; only a user submission carries\nduplicate-match metadata. Both import paths\nalso <strong><a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#exact-text-dedupe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">dedupe</a> by exact (normalized) text</strong> — against every existing fact row\nwith that text, active or not, and against every review still waiting on a\ndecision — before inserting anything, so re-running the same import twice,\nimporting a fact someone already submitted, or importing a fact that used to\nbe live and was later taken down, all queue nothing new for the ones that\nmatch. This is a narrower check than the submitter's duplicate warning: it\ncatches identical (post-normalization) text, not a reworded near-duplicate,\nand it silently skips rather than flagging for a human — there's no\nmoderator-style judgment call to make on an exact match. The admin-console\npath is interactive: the admin sees a skipped-as-duplicate count whenever a\nrun actually skips any. The API-key path is the one actually meant to run\nunattended.</p>\n<p><strong>Importing only loads the review queue — it never publishes anything.</strong>\nAn imported fact is exactly as unpublished as a hand-submitted one; it\nstill has to clear every gate in <a href=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\"><code>3-moderation.md</code></a> before\nit goes live.</p>\n<h3 id=\"near-duplicates-one-fact-per-joke\">Near-duplicates: one fact per joke</h3>\n<p>A moderator at <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#triage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">Triage</a> sees the\nduplicate check's verdict on the submission's saved wording — \"Duplicate of\n#N\", \"Duplicate of pending review #N\", \"Not a duplicate\", \"Couldn't check\" or\n\"Not checked yet\" — never a similarity percentage. A percentage measured how\nclose two sentences sit in an embedding space, which is not the question: a\nplural and a full stop scored an obvious duplicate at 77%. The verdict comes\nfrom an AI judgement of \"same fact or joke?\" on the closest few facts, and\nwhen the check can't run the screen says so and shows the closest fact rather\nthan guessing. A review with no verdict yet — one from before verdicts were\nstored, or a bulk import — is checked the first time it's opened. The\nmoderator has two choices: reject the\nsubmission as a duplicate, or accept it as a fact of its own. A different\nwording of a joke that's already live is the same joke, so the usual call is\nthe first. Every fact stands alone: nothing links one fact to another, and\neach fact earns its own classification, gags, images, votes and comments\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/decisions.md#2026-11-15--variants-are-retired-every-fact-stands-alone-and-the-existing-ones-are-deleted\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">why</a>).</p>\n<h3 id=\"underneath-one-funnel-one-cost-gate\">Underneath: one funnel, one cost gate</h3>\n<p>Every route in — the submit route and both import routes — calls the same function to create a pending review row, and nothing\nelse in the codebase does. That row starts at the very first stage\nof the review pipeline; no route can hand a fact a head start.\nThe <strong><a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#moderation-prep\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">moderation-prep pipeline</a></strong> — AI classification, no\nrenders yet — never runs at intake; that work only begins once a human moderator\nprovisionally accepts a submission at Triage. (The cheap pre-submit\naffordances a submitter already used on the way in — the grammar/<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#tokenize\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">tokenize</a>\npass, the duplicate check, hashtag suggestions — do call utility models;\n<a href=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\"><code>3-moderation.md</code></a> draws this same distinction. What's\ngated at Triage is the paid moderation-prep pipeline specifically, not every\nmodel call ever made about the fact.) Intake itself is just: normalize the\ngrammar and queue the review — a duplicate check runs on some routes (the\nsubmitter's own advisory check, the import routes' exact-text dedupe).\nSee <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/moderation-workflow.md#why-staged-moderation-exists\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>moderation-workflow.md</code></a>\nfor what happens from there, and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/moderation-workflow.md#the-ingestion-funnel--one-entrance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>moderation-workflow.md</code>'s ingestion-funnel section</a>\nfor the funnel itself.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-it-works-this-way\">Why it works this way</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>One funnel, so \"every fact gets reviewed\" is actually true.</strong> If\nsubmission and import each wrote to the facts table\nin their own way, \"nothing goes live without review\" would be separate\npromises to keep in sync instead of one function to trust. Routing every\nroute through the same primitive means a change to how review starts —\na new required field, a new starting stage — only has to be made once and\nis automatically true for every way a fact can arrive. See\n<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/decisions.md#2026-07-23--fact-lifecycle-closed-one-entrance-one-exit--activation-is-moderation-only-and-deactivation-is-reversible-through-moderation-not-a-direct-toggle\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">Fact lifecycle closed: one entrance, one exit</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>The duplicate check at submission warns; it doesn't refuse.</strong> A\nsame-meaning fact phrased differently is a legitimate call for a human to\nmake, not a machine — if the check catches it and finishes in time, the\nsubmitter sees the possible match and decides whether to send it anyway,\nand a moderator sees the same flag at Triage. Blocking automatically would\neither reject jokes that only look alike or need the exact wording match\nbulk import uses, which is far too blunt for something a human wrote from scratch. It\nruns best-effort rather than being made to block Submit for the same\nreason it isn't a hard gate at all — the cost of occasionally missing a\nflag is lower than the cost of holding up every submission on an AI call\nthat isn't authoritative anyway.</li>\n<li><strong>Bulk import's dedupe is exact-text and silent, because there's no\njudgment call to make on an exact match.</strong> An automated re-run of the same\nimport, or a second import that overlaps with an earlier, already-finished\none, is the normal case this guards — the match is unambiguous, so there's\nnothing for a human to weigh either way, whether or not one is actually\nwatching. A stricter, silent, exact match fits that; a softer semantic\ncheck that occasionally guesses wrong would not. (The check happens before\nthe insert, not as a database constraint, so it guards sequential runs —\ntwo imports racing at the exact same instant could each pass it before\neither has written anything; see <em>Boundaries</em> below.)</li>\n<li><strong>Grammar normalization runs again at the server, even though the client\nalready showed a preview of it.</strong> The preview is for the submitter's\nbenefit; the server-side pass is what actually determines what gets\nstored, so a submission that skipped the client (any path other than the\nstandard form) can't reach the queue with an unexpanded token or an\nun-conjugated verb.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"boundaries--known-limitations\">Boundaries &#x26; known limitations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Duplicate detection is advisory, not a gate.</strong> A submitter can send a\nfact flagged as a likely duplicate; nothing stops them, and nothing stops a\nmoderator from approving it anyway if they disagree with the verdict. The\nAI stage compares against live facts only: another pending submission is\ncaught only when its wording is identical (case, spacing and punctuation\naside).</li>\n<li><strong>Bulk import's dedupe only catches exact, post-normalization text.</strong> Two\nimports of the same fact queue separately unless they normalize to\nidentical stored text — a trailing-space or grammar-cleanup difference can\nstill collapse to the same match and get caught; a difference that\nsurvives normalization does not.</li>\n<li><strong>Bulk import's dedupe is a same-request guard, not a database\nconstraint.</strong> It checks before it writes rather than relying on a\nuniqueness rule the database itself enforces, so two imports that overlap\nby coincidence — not one waiting for the other to finish — can each pass\nthe check before either has inserted, and both queue.</li>\n<li><strong>A submitter's own pending facts are protected from flooding the review\nqueue</strong> — see <code>artifacts/api-server/src/lib/rateLimit.ts</code> for how.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"going-deeper\">Going deeper</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Spec: <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/moderation-workflow.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>moderation-workflow.md</code></a> — the\n<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#ingestion-funnel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">ingestion funnel</a>, the activation chokepoint, and everything that happens\nto a fact after it's queued.</li>\n<li>Related: <a href=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\"><code>3-moderation.md</code></a> (the three-gate review a\nqueued fact goes through), <a href=\"/admin/help/4-taxonomy-and-enrichment\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/4-taxonomy-and-enrichment\"><code>4-taxonomy-and-enrichment.md</code></a>\n(what a fact's classification means and how it's produced), and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/architecture-map.md#async-jobs-and-queues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>architecture-map.md</code></a>\n(the async <a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/glossary.md#lane\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\">lanes</a> that run a fact's prep work once it's accepted).</li>\n<li>Rationale: the fact-lifecycle entries in\n<a href=\"https://github.com/TheAnswerManIsHere/Overhypeme/blob/main/docs/ai-context/decisions.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-external=\"true\"><code>decisions.md</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Next:</strong> chapter 3 — <a href=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\" data-help-internal=\"/admin/help/3-moderation\"><code>3-moderation.md</code></a>, the three human\ngates a queued fact walks through before it can go live.</p>\n<p><em>Verified against <code>b720d6f</code> (2026-08-08) · claim inventory in PR #355. The\nnear-duplicate section rewritten when the link between facts was retired\n(2026-11-15).</em></p>";
